--
N5008 [class.compare.default]/1-2: a defaulted comparison operator may be a
FRIEND of the class taking two `const C &' parameters; it is defined as the
memberwise comparison ([class.eq]/2) exactly like the defaulted member form
`bool operator==(const C &) const = default'.  The member form works; the
friend form fails with "symbol '' is unknown" at the declaration and the
translation unit is rejected.  This is libc++'s std::to_chars_result
(`friend bool operator==(const to_chars_result &, const to_chars_result &) =
default'), whose operator== body is dropped in every libc++ C++20 test
(audit residue item 3, round 162).
